project/game-fsm-builder: ctx.defineGameFSM(spec) in apps/_lib/game-fsm.js compiles a declarative spec into an xstate5 machine (setup({guards,actions}).createMachine + createActor) for game-phase orchestration. Spec: {initial, context, states:{name:{enter(ctx,fsm), exit, tick(ctx,dt,fsm), on:{EVT:target|{target,guard,action}}, after:{ms:target|[{target,guard}...]}, final}}}. Runtime: state/context/timeInState/is/matches/can/send/onTransition/tick/stop. fsm.context IS the live xstate context (mutate fsm.context.x++ visible immediately to guards). App drives via update(ctx,dt)->fsm.tick(dt) (only active state ticks; final stops). Surfaced on AppContext (src/apps/AppContext.js) next to createMachine(); lifecycle.js stays the app-level machine. Multi-target after arrays = ordered guard candidates, first passing wins, bare last = fall-through (this needed normalizeTransition array handling). Server+client (singleplayer BrowserServer) via _isNode ? xstate : /node_modules/xstate dual-import. Example apps/fsm-arena; create-app --template fsm-game; tests apps/_lib/game-fsm.test.js via npm test (14 pass); browser-witnessed import in singleplayer.